{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.AomegaM2BPSCohomology"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.dt_output_bar_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.dt_output_bar_split","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.lean#L72-L79","doc":"Conditional consequence: the bar split of any M3-identified category is\nthe certified `(7, 1)` — even part `7`, odd part `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.dt_output_four_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.dt_output_four_three","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.lean#L64-L70","doc":"Conditional consequence: any category satisfying M3 outputs the concrete\nchirality pair `(4, 3)` — composed from the class fields and M2's decidable\nanchors, so the identification inherits every certified M2 number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.IdentifiesClosedSector.dt_minus_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.IdentifiesClosedSector.dt_minus_eq","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The `S⁻`-sector output equals the certified `dimBPSminus`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.IdentifiesClosedSector.dt_plus_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.IdentifiesClosedSector.dt_plus_eq","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The `S⁺`-sector output equals the certified `dimBPSplus`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.IdentifiesClosedSector.dtOutput","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.IdentifiesClosedSector.dtOutput","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.lean#L58-L58","doc":"`C` has a well-defined chirality-graded integer DT output (Int — the ℤ notation is outside this import cone). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.IdentifiesClosedSector.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.IdentifiesClosedSector.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.IdentifiesClosedSector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.IdentifiesClosedSector","kind":"class","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RouteCM3CategoryIdentification.lean#L49-L62","doc":"**M3 (primary conjecture).** The closed-sector categorical datum `C`\ncarries a chirality-graded DT output (`true` = the `S⁺` sector, `false` =\n`S⁻`) that reproduces the certified M2 spectrum. Content-bearing: the two\nequations are the conjecture's falsifiable claims about `C`; an instance\nexists iff the identification holds for `C`. (Carries the `dtOutput` data\nfield, so it is a data-class, not a `Prop` marker — deliberately: an\ninstance must SUPPLY the output, not merely assert one exists.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}